{
  "_README": [
    "Plan 2 name sets. Each name: Latin form, katakana form (ja), Cyrillic nominative form (ru).",
    "'alts' lists other renderings accepted for exact match (the dataset's own variants, or",
    "common standard variants). The FIRST form is the reference for log-prob and edit distance.",
    "",
    "set a = the two forget01 authors. ja/ru references are the dataset's majority forms;",
    "        alts are the other renderings that occur in forget01 itself (copy_check.py, Step 0).",
    "set b = 20 retain99 authors, forms taken from the majority rendering in retain99_ja /",
    "        retain99_ru (Russian: the nominative). NOT a neutral control: every unlearning arm's",
    "        retain term trained on these authors IN ITS OWN LANGUAGE.",
    "set c = names unrelated to TOFU. tags: real (has a standard published rendering) vs",
    "        invented (reference is a hand-made transliteration; read transliteration tasks on",
    "        these as change vs fr_ft, not as correctness); overlap = shares a name piece with",
    "        a forget author (Basil / Mahfouz / Al-Kuwaiti / Nikolai / Nikola), which separates",
    "        'general skill damaged' from 'shared word forms damaged' (Stage 6). native_cyrillic",
    "        = the person's own name is Cyrillic, so Latin->Cyrillic is recall, not transliteration.",
    "",
    "Hand-authored 2026-10-21. A fluent ja/ru reader should check set c's katakana/Cyrillic."
